they approached the producers of the primetime television program Unsolved Mysteries. As well as featuring stories about missing persons and unexplained paranormal phenomena, the series explored unsolved crimes. Viewers at home were encouraged to call in to the show's hotline with any information they might have. The show's producers were keen to cover the Omar fire. Some of the case investigators, including Doug Allen and Frank Curry appeared on camera to discuss their concerns. The show also depicted a reenactment of how the mysterious and disturbing videotape was found.
