the existence of a creepy video of the entire thing came as a disturbing surprise. He called the Unsolved Mysteries Hotline, Ed wasn't the only viewer who recognised the property. Bill Otterley was a contractor who'd struggled with constructing a house back in the summer of 1988. The residence he had been building was a 4,200 square foot home in Redwood City's Emerald Lake Hills neighbourhood. It was an expensive undertaking, with the house valued at $850,000. Just after the home's plywood wall, were put up, the entire thing was burned down under the cover of night.
但存在一段关于整件事的恐怖视频是一个令人不安的惊喜。他拨打了《未解之谜》热线，埃德并不是唯一认出该房产的观众。比尔·奥特利是一位承包商，他在1988年夏天曾为建造一栋房子而苦恼。他正在建造的住宅是红木城翡翠湖山社区一栋4200平方英尺的房子。这是一项昂贵的工程，房屋价值85万美元。就在房子的胶合板墙立起来后，整栋房子在夜幕掩护下被烧毁了。

19
00:13:59.000 --> 00:15:03.000
When Bill discovered what had happened, he had sat by the destroyed shell of a house and cried. The house was rebuilt, and during the second attempt at construction, Bill had paid an employee to stand guard over it at night. As Bill watched Unsolved Mysteries air footage of the fire that had stumped arson investigators over in Stockton, he recognised their house being destroyed by flames. He was watching his own property burn to the ground. In the days after the episode aired, the team at Unsolved Mysteries received a record-breaking 1,600 phone calls. Some offered theories about where the patch sewn on the fatigue jacket had originated from, or what it signified. Others called in from all over the country to report house fires they thought matched the one on the Stockton Arsoness tape.
当比尔发现发生了什么事时，他坐在被毁的房屋外壳旁哭泣。房子被重建了，在第二次施工尝试期间，比尔雇了一名员工在晚上守卫它。当比尔观看《未解之谜》播出斯托克顿纵火调查人员一直无法解决的火灾画面时，他认出了他们被火焰摧毁的房子。他正在看着自己的房产被烧成灰烬。在剧集播出后的几天里，《未解之谜》团队收到了创纪录的1600个电话。一些人提供了关于迷彩夹克上缝制的徽章起源或其含义的理论。其他人从全国各地打来电话，报告他们认为与斯托克顿纵火犯录像带相符的房屋火灾。

